What-If Tool:
https://pair-code.github.io/what-if-tool/demos/uci.html
This demo loads two binary classifiers trained on real US Census data. Each model predicts whether a
person earns more or less than $50K/year, based on attributes like age, education, occupation, hours
worked, marital status, race, and sex. The demo lets you compare two differently trained models side
by side on the same individuals.

COMPAS recidivism risk model:
https://pair-code.github.io/what-if-tool/demos/compas.html
This demo loads a classifier that mimics COMPAS, a real risk-assessment tool that has been used by
US courts to help decide bail, sentencing, and parole. It predicts whether a defendant is Low risk or
Medium/High risk of reoffending, based on their criminal history and demographics. COMPAS is the
system at the center of ProPublica's landmark 2016 investigation "Machine Bias" and the Wisconsin
Supreme Court case State v. Loomis — both essential background if you want to cite real precedent
in your presentation.
